# Line endings.
#
# NUDO is checked out, edited and compared on Windows, Linux and macOS, and the
# conformance corpus is compared line by line. A platform-dependent line ending
# would make the same commit produce different results on different machines,
# which is precisely the property a conformance corpus must not have.
#
# Everything is normalised to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
# The lexer accepts CRLF as a line terminator, so a source file that arrives
# with CRLF still lexes to the same positions.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Source, corpus and configuration are compared as text.
*.nudo  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.ebnf  text eol=lf
*.rs    text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one exception: Windows tooling reads it with a CRLF
# convention, and nothing in this repository compares these files as text.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary
